{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}_x = \\mathcal{F}_x^{ext}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:996426542333db316a5b35a9b759a71361d78440524d5280d8547a1f02af9dd7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8191aa5347b0b012e9b19cdd3f81ae865cb9eaf1adc71e4287007fb82a65034b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that we have\n<MATH_0001>\nas <MATH_0002>-modules in the situation of the lemma.\nThis is so because the collection of elements of <MATH_0003> containing\n<MATH_0004> forms a fundamental system of open neighbourhoods of <MATH_0005>, or\nsimply because it is true on the underlying sets.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d3532ea2897401fe281270c205efc22ca2fc9fcddbad67c7b4007f1fc6bd2cfa", "unit_id": "tag:009H:prose-0011"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}|_\\mathcal{B})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}|_\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}|_\\mathcal{B})\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{B}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-restrict-basis-equivalence-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d57bc2284c8675e8bc01ad494136a84cbade0fac521e22dfd44a965feffbb902", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:24aecaf3a44610c037fb3694d3307ca17bff4095ceb36729288936f526214cda", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a basis for the topology on <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf of rings on <MATH_0005>.\nDenote <MATH_0006> the category of\nsheaves of <MATH_0007>-modules on <MATH_0008>.\nThere is an equivalence of categories\n<MATH_0009>\nwhich assigns to a sheaf of <MATH_0010>-modules on <MATH_0011> its restriction to\nthe members of <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:acaa7121ae35c938987234f518864a46d449f6ccbea7d07dd6d3f11779c5799b", "unit_id": "tag:009U:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-extend-off-basis-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fb683870524c7c5d1f1202c31d76a82e8babca7e93cad7c7a3d1adebfaa9acb3", "source_text": "The inverse functor in given in\nLemma <REF_0001> above.\nChecking the obvious functorialities is left to the reader.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:31cbd7bd06fe6728ed876ead619831caad1c8358c2b44bcb92ef580c51445f76", "unit_id": "tag:009U:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0735b88cea6d958336921db5f0798d8e6d4c98e15270f97bb396102542b9c955", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFinally, we address the question of the relationship of this with\ncontinuous maps. This is now very easy thanks to the work\nabove. First we do the case where there is a basis on the\ntarget given.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ef9c29c67b0033f7d099581ad37e6f28661e0de67aa8c5733f28cbc6e0c8d496", "unit_id": "tag:009H:prose-0012"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\mathcal{C}, F)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0010": "$Y$", "MATH_0011": "$V \\in \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\varphi_V :\n\\mathcal{G}(V)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V)\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$f$", "MATH_0016": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\varphi_V$", "MATH_0018": "$V \\in \\mathcal{B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-f-map}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-presheaves-structures-functorial}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-f-map-basis-below-structures}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:408602b133d2868d5af609329eb845d7c7233dea3dc86f2f3dfadd57753aa8e8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ffd5fb08fe05584b4546359445b37efa577ac15786edf9ad5529726a2ca74dd6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a type of algebraic structures.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a sheaf with values in <MATH_0004> on <MATH_0005>.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a sheaf with values in <MATH_0007> on <MATH_0008>.\nLet <MATH_0009> be a basis for the topology on <MATH_0010>.\nSuppose given for every <MATH_0011> a morphism\n<MATH_0012>\nof <MATH_0013> compatible with restriction mappings.\nThen there is a unique <MATH_0014>-map (see Definition <REF_0001>\nand discussion of <MATH_0015>-maps in\nSection <REF_0002>)\n<MATH_0016>\nrecovering <MATH_0017> for <MATH_0018>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3213406b0ea0125759642596d13cb486d80f548ebff3e8698851a90a08493af5", "unit_id": "tag:009V:statement"}
